      "id": "GENUS_BOMBYCILLA",
      "name": "Bombycilla",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Plump crested silky-plumaged birds named for the red wax-like tips on their secondary feathers. They breed in boreal Sweden's spruce-birch forest, subsisting on berries and insects. In winter they irrupt southward when the northern rowan crop fails — a waxwing invasion stripping Stockholm's ornamental rowans is one of the great Scandinavian winter spectacles.",
      "lineage": "Waxwings",
